WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.763
Reconcile the finished artifact with the original charter.

00:00:03.355 --> 00:00:06.467
In the fictional intake example, the revised tabletop

00:00:06.525 --> 00:00:10.925
supports complete-input review, visible missing-date handling, and an

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:14.187
approval gate that keeps delivery blocked. Keep the

00:00:14.245 --> 00:00:16.462
before and after correction and the three test

00:00:16.532 --> 00:00:20.019
observations beside that claim. The example has not

00:00:20.077 --> 00:00:23.711
established live delivery, integration, measured time savings, or

00:00:23.792 --> 00:00:27.937
customer benefit. A dashboard remains outside scope. These

00:00:27.983 --> 00:00:31.141
limits belong in the explanation. Save the finished

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:34.670
version, evidence trail, and scope reconciliation in the

00:00:34.717 --> 00:00:38.235
Capstone Integration Package and connected workbook. Show the

00:00:38.293 --> 00:00:42.084
finished result and a before-and-after correction. Explain why

00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:44.046
it satisfies the charter and what it has

00:00:44.127 --> 00:00:47.634
not yet established. If a required criterion still

00:00:47.703 --> 00:00:50.443
fails, keep it pending and repair it before

00:00:50.490 --> 00:00:53.682
claiming completion. Carry the same package into the

00:00:53.729 --> 00:00:54.820
next readiness review.
